+## firing it out of the store
+
+A show is designed against the house catalog and fired out of whatever the
+magazine holds, and those are never the same list. Hand any show command the
+magazine book and every cue is drawn from a real lot, in firing order, so the
+sheet names the case the crew has to open:
+
+```
+portfire sheet show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine book.csv
+portfire check show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine book.csv \
+  --pull vn2405,vn2413
+```
+
+`--pull` sets lots aside first, which is what a recall or a damaged case means.
+A cue the stock cannot reach is covered by the nearest thing the store holds:
+the same calibre first, a shell in the same handling band second, and a note or
+a warning either way. Nothing covers it and the show is not ready. The order
+list `inventory` prints still counts what the script asked for, because a
+stand-in is how a show gets fired on the day and not a reason to stop ordering
+the shell the design wants.
+
 A worked example lives in `examples/autumn`.
 
